The task is finished. The anthropic and bedrock arms now show the guessed-limits warning, and #1021 has a comment with the results and the commit sha. The interrupted earlier run had already committed the code as 4c29bbc6. What it hadn't done was post that comment, so the ticket's latest word was still the pre-fix one from 2026-10-24.

Checks rerun this session: cargo fmt --check, cargo clippy --all-targets -D warnings and cargo test all pass (27 test binaries, 0 failures). The working tree is clean, so there was nothing new to commit.

What the commit does: all 4 arms of build_agent now call warn_once_if_guessing; before, only 2 did. I checked which model ids warn before wiring it in, and the existing check needed no change:

| provider | model id | warns? |
|---|---|---|
| anthropic | claude-opus-5-5 (my loop's model and the no-config default) | no, it has real declared limits |
| anthropic | claude-made-up-9 | yes |
| bedrock | anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6 (the bedrock default) | yes |
| bedrock | amazon.nova-pro-v1:0 | yes |

The bedrock default warning is correct, because bedrock has no presets and every bedrock id runs on guessed limits. I didn't move the threshold to keep it quiet.

One change from the plan: the task asked for a real-binary check using --print-system-prompt. That flag never builds the agent, so it shows no warning for either id and can't tell them apart. The real-binary test runs -p against a local stub server instead.

Still open on #1021: giving the bedrock default real limits (the next slice), and item (1), the gemini-2.x ids.

